{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-07_11-29-07-hashicorp_raft-real-run && cat research.json'","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"audit_spec_path\": \"/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-07_11-29-07-hashicorp_raft-real-run/audit-spec/v1.json\",\n  \"audit_spec_version\": 1,\n  \"activity_roles\": {\n    \"A1\": {\n      \"role\": \"core\",\n      \"relation\": \"Qualified support for decision formation and legal advancement\"\n    },\n    \"A2\": {\n      \"role\": \"core\",\n      \"relation\": \"Context validity and acquisition, transfer or loss of authority\"\n    },\n    \"A3\": {\n      \"role\": \"support\",\n      \"relation\": \"Recovery and resynchronization of eligible participation\"\n    },\n    \"A4\": {\n      \"role\": \"support\",\n      \"relation\": \"Configuration and participant eligibility\"\n    },\n    \"A5\": {\n      \"role\": \"support\",\n      \"relation\": \"Decision application and consumption\"\n    },\n    \"A6\": {\n      \"role\": \"support\",\n      \"relation\": \"History, persistence and reconstruction of support\"\n    },\n    \"A7\": {\n      \"role\": \"support\",\n      \"relation\": \"Client contracts, invocation intervals and observed completion\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"activity_focus\": [],\n  \"understanding_status\": \"usable\",\n  \"core_overview\": {\n    \"formation\": {\n      \"explanation\": \"Qualified support is gathered before a decision is formed. A candidate counts granted votes (or pre-vote grants) and only becomes leader when the count reaches quorumSize(); the leader then records each voter's acknowledged match index through commitment.match, and commitment.recalculate advances commitIndex only when the majority match index is at least commitment.startIndex, the first index created in the leader's own term, so entries of earlier terms are never committed on match indexes alone. Followers advance their own commit index only from the leader's LeaderCommitIndex bounded by their own last index.\",\n      \"behavior_ids\": [\n        \"b-elect-self\",\n        \"b-vote-grant\",\n        \"b-replication-ack\",\n        \"b-commit-advance\",\n        \"b-follower-commit-advance\",\n        \"b-follower-append-entries\"\n      ],\n      \"fact_ids\": [\n        \"f-follower-log-state\",\n        \"f-follower-match\",\n        \"f-commit-index\"\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"s-raft-candidate-vote\",\n        \"s-raft-candidate-prevote\",\n        \"s-raft-vote-record\",\n        \"s-commitment-core\",\n        \"s-commitment-recalc\",\n        \"s-replication-ack\",\n        \"s-raft-append-commit\",\n        \"s-raft-append-entries-log\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"context\": {\n      \"explanation\": \"The context that qualifies support and authority is the adopted term plus the known leader identity. Inbound AppendEntries/RequestVote/InstallSnapshot ignore older terms and adopt a strictly greater one by writing StableStore and dropping to Follower; accepted AppendEntries/InstallSnapshot then record the leader identity, which requestVote/requestPreVote use to refuse support while a different leader is known. A leader loses authority locally through checkLeaderLease when it cannot contact a quorum of voters within LeaderLeaseTimeout, and gains it at the target through TimeoutNow, which puts the target into Candidate with candidateFromLeadershipTransfer. The same term/leader update is additionally reachable from a NetworkTransport connection goroutine through the registered heartbeat callback.\",\n      \"behavior_ids\": [\n        \"b-term-observation\",\n        \"b-leader-identity\",\n        \"b-heartbeat-fastpath\",\n        \"b-leader-lease-stepdown\",\n        \"b-timeout-now-transfer\"\n      ],\n      \"fact_ids\": [\n        \"f-term-adopted\",\n        \"f-known-leader\"\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"s-raft-append-term\",\n        \"s-raft-append-leader\",\n        \"s-raft-set-state\",\n        \"s-raft-set-current-term\",\n        \"s-raft-process-heartbeat\",\n        \"s-net-fastpath\",\n        \"s-net-handle-conn\",\n        \"s-api-fastpath-contract\",\n        \"s-raft-leader-lease\",\n        \"s-raft-timeout-now\",\n        \"s-raft-request-vote-filter\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"connection\": {\n      \"explanation\": \"The two lines meet at the term and at the own-term replication rule. A durable vote record is only re-granted for the same (term, candidate) and is otherwise superseded once a greater term is adopted, so support gathered in term T cannot be consumed in term T+1; conversely an RPC whose term is older than the adopted term is ignored, so a deposed leader cannot re-establish authority. On the leader side, a follower's match index only becomes usable support after the leader has matched a quorum at or beyond commitment.startIndex, so pending work from an earlier term constrains what the new leader may commit; and leadership transfer explicitly requires the target's nextIndex to be past the leader's lastIndex before TimeoutNow, so an up-to-date support context is a precondition for moving authority. Because both lines read and write the same current-term context, an entry point that updates that context outside the main goroutine (the transport heartbeat callback) is the point where the connection is not obviously serialized.\",\n      \"behavior_ids\": [\n        \"b-commit-advance\",\n        \"b-term-observation\",\n        \"b-follower-append-entries\",\n        \"b-timeout-now-transfer\",\n        \"b-replication-ack\"\n      ],\n      \"fact_ids\": [\n        \"f-term-adopted\",\n        \"f-commit-index\",\n        \"f-follower-match\"\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"s-commitment-core\",\n        \"s-commitment-recalc\",\n        \"s-raft-append-term\",\n        \"s-raft-set-current-term\",\n        \"s-raft-append-entries-log\",\n        \"s-raft-append-config\",\n        \"s-raft-leadership-transfer\",\n        \"s-raft-timeout-now\",\n        \"s-replication-ack\",\n        \"s-replication-replicateTo\",\n        \"s-raft-dispatch-logs\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"open_details\": [\n      \"The pre-vote grant path was read at the level needed for the context path; its interaction with a concurrently observed leader was not traced to completion.\",\n      \"Verification reads (VerifyLeader/verifyFuture) and their quorum accounting were not traced to completion; they are represented only through the client contract activity.\",\n      \"Snapshot-driven log truncation was read at its call sites; the interaction with a MonotonicLogStore implementation is recorded as a deferred surface.\"\n    ],\n    \"core_gaps\": [],\n    \"status\": \"usable\",\n    \"rationale\": \"Both core relationships and their connection are explained from actual code: formation and advancement are grounded in the vote tally, the pre-vote round, commitment.match/recalculate and the startIndex own-term rule; context and authority are grounded in the term/state update, leader identity update, the leader lease step-down and TimeoutNow. The connection is sourced: votes are only re-granted for the same term, older-term RPCs are ignored, match indexes are only usable at or after startIndex, and a transfer requires the target to be caught up. The one anomaly found while reading this backbone (the transport heartbeat callback that re-uses appendEntries from a connection goroutine) is recorded as a Behavior unknown and as the first Candidate rather than as a core gap, so the overview remains usable while that premise stays open.\"\n  },\n  \"understanding_changes\": [\n    {\n      \"operation_id\": \"8c760622d9ac4b608865bde2e03830a7\",\n      \"version\": 1,\n      \"record\": {\n        \"path\": \"state.json\",\n        \"collection\": \"selections\",\n        \"match\": {\n          \"operation_id\": \"8c760622d9ac4b608865bde2e03830a7\"\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"next_objective\": {\n    \"action\": \"investigate_and_refocus\",\n    \"boundary\": \"both_core_paths\",\n    \"reason\": \"Use results to update understanding and compare the remaining frontier\",\n    \"core_gaps\": []\n  },\n  \"drafts\": [],\n  \"candidates\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"0282b98964724def801bc4da741e6112\",\n      \"question\": {\n        \"audit_spec_version\": 1,\n        \"disposition\": \"ready_for_check\",\n        \"preferred_check\": \"direct_test\",\n        \"question\": \"Does the transport heartbeat callback establish the election-term and known-leader context under the same serialization as the raft main goroutine, i.e. can Raft.processHeartbeat run on a NetworkTransport connection goroutine concurrently with main-goroutine RPC handling and store a current term lower than a term the node has already adopted, or replace the currently known leader?\",\n        \"importance\": \"The adopted current term is the value against which vote granting, duplicate-vote rejection and the acceptance of newer-term RPCs are all evaluated. If a heartbeat handled off the main goroutine stores a term lower than one the node has already adopted, the node can subsequently grant a vote in a term in which it has already voted, which is the election-safety condition of Raft; the same entry point also rewrites the stored leader identity that clients and requestVote rely on. The packaged NetworkTransport/TCPStreamLayer is the production transport, so the path is on the default deployment and not only in tests.\",\n        \"source_ids\": [\n          \"s-raft-append-term\",\n          \"s-raft-append-leader\",\n          \"s-raft-set-current-term\",\n          \"s-raft-set-state\",\n          \"s-state-term-atomic\",\n          \"s-raft-process-heartbeat\",\n          \"s-net-fastpath\",\n          \"s-net-handle-conn\",\n          \"s-net-set-heartbeat\",\n          \"s-api-fastpath-contract\",\n          \"s-transport-interface\",\n          \"s-integ-fastpath\",\n          \"s-raft-vote-record\",\n          \"s-raft-request-vote-filter\",\n          \"s-commitment-core\",\n          \"s-commitment-recalc\",\n          \"s-raft-dispatch-logs\"\n        ],\n        \"participants\": [\n          \"NetworkTransport connection goroutine (handleCommand heartbeat fast path)\",\n          \"Raft main goroutine (run -> processRPC)\",\n          \"Raft.processHeartbeat\",\n          \"Raft.appendEntries\",\n          \"StableStore CurrentTerm\"\n        ],\n        \"objects\": [\n          \"Raft.raftState.currentTerm\",\n          \"Raft.raftState.state\",\n          \"Raft.leaderAddr/leaderID\",\n          \"NetworkTransport.heartbeatFn\",\n          \"commitment.startIndex\",\n          \"StableStore LastVoteTerm/LastVoteCand\"\n        ],\n        \"contexts\": [\n          \"a node in Follower state, with a heartbeat handler registered by NewRaft, receiving a heartbeat-shaped AppendEntries from a leader of term T over NetworkTransport while the main goroutine handles another RPC\",\n          \"a NetworkTransport whose connection-handler goroutine invokes the callback while the main goroutine is inside appendEntries or requestVote\"\n        ],\n        \"event_paths\": [\n          \"connection goroutine: handleConn -> handleCommand (isHeartbeat) -> heartbeatFn(rpc) -> Raft.processHeartbeat -> Raft.appendEntries -> setState/setCurrentTerm/setLeader\",\n          \"main goroutine: run -> rpcCh -> processRPC -> appendEntries (setState/setCurrentTerm/setLeader) or requestVote (setState/setCurrentTerm/persistVote)\",\n          \"vote reuse path: requestVote reads LastVoteTerm/LastVoteCand and re-grants only for the same (term, candidate), else persists a new vote for req.Term\"\n        ],\n        \"activity_classes\": [\n          \"A2\"\n        ],\n        \"behavior_ids\": [\n          \"b-term-observation\",\n          \"b-heartbeat-fastpath\",\n          \"b-vote-grant\"\n        ],\n        \"fact_ids\": [\n          \"f-term-adopted\"\n        ],\n        \"supporting_behavior_ids\": {\n          \"b-leader-identity\": \"the same fast-path entry point also writes the known-leader context, which is the sibling fact consumed by vote-grant filtering and by the client API\",\n          \"b-commit-advance\": \"shows which later decisions depend on the adopted term context by gating commitment on commitment.startIndex\"\n        },\n        \"obligation_relation_kind\": \"preservation\",\n        \"counterevidence\": [\n          \"The heartbeat classification keeps the fast path to requests with PrevLogEntry==0, PrevLogTerm==0, no Entries and LeaderCommitIndex==0, so it cannot append log entries, advance the commit index or run processLogs, which bounds the reachable damage.\",\n          \"currentTerm is read and written with atomic LoadUint64/StoreUint64 on raftState, so the hazard is a lost update (read-modify-write) rather than a plain unsynchronized access to that specific field; state and leaderAddr/leaderID are also individually atomic or lock-protected.\",\n          \"InmemTransport ignores SetHeartbeatHandler and always offers AppendEntries to the consumer channel, so in-memory clusters do not exercise the fast path; the integ_test.go pre-vote test installs a custom handler that itself calls processHeartbeat, which shows the pattern is used but does not establish a legal interleaving.\",\n          \"The heartbeat fast path is documented as existing to avoid head-of-line blocking from disk IO, i.e. to be concurrent by design; if the concurrent dispatch is intentional, the defect would be that appendEntries does not uphold the stated requirement rather than that the dispatch exists.\"\n        ],\n        \"unknowns\": [\n          \"Whether the connection goroutine and the main goroutine can actually interleave between the currentTerm read and the setCurrentTerm write on the same node in a legal history, and therefore whether a lower term can be stored after a higher one.\",\n          \"Whether a stored-term regression, if reachable, can be escalated to two votes in one term given the LastVoteTerm/LastVoteCand duplicate check, or is bounded to a transient context error.\",\n          \"Whether NetworkTransport is expected to serialize connection goroutines with the raft main goroutine at all, or whether the requirement in api.go only means the callback must not block on the main goroutine's disk IO.\",\n          \"Whether the same premise exists for other transport implementations that honour SetHeartbeatHandler, since only the in-module NetworkTransport path was read.\"\n        ],\n        \"priority\": 3,\n        \"trigger_rationale\": \"Three sourced facts point at this premise and conflict: api.go states a requirement that the heartbeat callback MUST be safe to be called concurrently with a blocking RPC; raft.go's processHeartbeat comment states the opposite, that it must only be called from the main thread; and NetworkTransport.handleCommand invokes the registered callback directly on a per-connection goroutine while non-heartbeat RPCs are serialized through the single rpcCh consumer. appendEntries performs a read-compare-write on currentTerm through a plain atomic Store (no compare-and-swap) and then unconditionally rewrites the leader identity, so the premise is a concrete interleaving question rather than a generic concurrency caution.\"\n      },\n      \"status\": \"escalated\",\n      \"parent_candidate_id\": null,\n      \"fork_reason\": \"\",\n      \"stop_reason\": \"First investigation of the captured hashicorp/raft snapshot (commit c0dc6a0b2c7e889f31e5ab2f7ed90ceb159acffe). It records a usable map of both core relationships (A1 qualified support for decision formation/advancement, A2 context validity and authority transfer/loss) and their connection, and fixes one obligation about the adopted-term context after finding that the network transport can drive the appendEntries term/leader update from a per-connection goroutine through the heartbeat callback. The question is registered as the first Candidate with its counterevidence and unknowns, so the obligation states a required relation without asserting a violation.\",\n      \"resume_conditions\": [],\n      \"obligation_id\": \"c-adopted-term-never-regresses\",\n      \"result_claim_ids\": [],\n      \"open_issue_ids\": [],\n      \"executions\": [],\n      \"record\": {\n        \"path\": \"state.json\",\n        \"collection\": \"question_candidates\",\n        \"match\": {\n          \"id\": \"0282b98964724def801bc4da741e6112\"\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"units\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"unit-c-adopted-term-never-regresses\",\n      \"candidate_id\": \"0282b98964724def801bc4da741e6112\",\n      \"obligation_ids\": [\n        \"c-adopted-term-never-regresses\"\n      ],\n      \"binding_ids\": [\n        \"bind-raft-process-heartbeat\"\n      ],\n      \"relation_ids\": [],\n      \"scope\": {\n        \"description\": \"A single Raft node using the in-module NetworkTransport (or any transport that honours SetHeartbeatHandler) with a heartbeat handler registered by NewRaft, while it is handling RPCs. Applies to the current-term context only, not to the log content, the commit index or the configuration.\",\n        \"assumptions\": [\n          \"the node is not shut down while the RPCs are processed\",\n          \"the StableStore accepts SetUint64 for the CurrentTerm key, since setCurrentTerm panics otherwise\",\n          \"an RPC with a term greater than the adopted term is a legal event, because appendEntries and requestVote adopt it\"\n        ],\n        \"excluded\": [\n          \"log replication correctness and the commit-index rule (a separate obligation)\",\n          \"the leader-identity fact, which is tracked separately as f-known-leader\",\n          \"behaviour of transports outside this module that do not implement a heartbeat fast path\"\n        ],\n        \"parameters\": {}\n      },\n      \"rationale\": \"First investigation of the captured hashicorp/raft snapshot (commit c0dc6a0b2c7e889f31e5ab2f7ed90ceb159acffe). It records a usable map of both core relationships (A1 qualified support for decision formation/advancement, A2 context validity and authority transfer/loss) and their connection, and fixes one obligation about the adopted-term context after finding that the network transport can drive the appendEntries term/leader update from a per-connection goroutine through the heartbeat callback. The question is registered as the first Candidate with its counterevidence and unknowns, so the obligation states a required relation without asserting a violation.\",\n      \"status\": \"pending\",\n      \"previous_id\": null,\n      \"version\": 1,\n      \"boundary_changes\": [],\n      \"obligation_checks\": {},\n      \"remaining_obligation_ids\": [\n        \"c-adopted-term-never-regresses\"\n      ],\n      \"recheck_reasons\": [],\n      \"coverage_limitations\": [],\n      \"progress\": [\n        {\n          \"claim_id\": \"c-adopted-term-never-regresses\",\n          \"record_status\": \"no_fixed_check\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"source_explanation\": null,\n      \"record\": {\n        \"path\": \"state.json\",\n        \"collection\": \"units\",\n        \"match\": {\n          \"id\": \"unit-c-adopted-term-never-regresses\",\n          \"version\": 1\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"claims\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c-adopted-term-never-regresses\",\n      \"kind\": \"obligation\",\n      \"concern\": \"consensus_safety\",\n      \"description\": \"Once a node has adopted and persisted election term T as its current term, no later establishment of that term context may store a value lower than T, because vote granting, duplicate-vote rejection and the acceptance of newer-term RPCs are all evaluated against the adopted value; the requirement applies to every entry point that can update the term context, including a heartbeat-shaped AppendEntries processed outside the raft main goroutine.\",\n      \"scope\": {\n        \"description\": \"A single Raft node using the in-module NetworkTransport (or any transport that honours SetHeartbeatHandler) with a heartbeat handler registered by NewRaft, while it is handling RPCs. Applies to the current-term context only, not to the log content, the commit index or the configuration.\",\n        \"assumptions\": [\n          \"the node is not shut down while the RPCs are processed\",\n          \"the StableStore accepts SetUint64 for the CurrentTerm key, since setCurrentTerm panics otherwise\",\n          \"an RPC with a term greater than the adopted term is a legal event, because appendEntries and requestVote adopt it\"\n        ],\n        \"excluded\": [\n          \"log replication correctness and the commit-index rule (a separate obligation)\",\n          \"the leader-identity fact, which is tracked separately as f-known-leader\",\n          \"behaviour of transports outside this module that do not implement a heartbeat fast path\"\n        ],\n        \"parameters\": {}\n      },\n      \"source\": \"Candidate derived from attributed implementation responsibilities\",\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"s-raft-append-term\",\n        \"s-raft-set-current-term\",\n        \"s-state-term-atomic\",\n        \"s-raft-vote-record\",\n        \"s-raft-process-heartbeat\",\n        \"s-api-fastpath-contract\"\n      ],\n      \"pending\": [\n        \"whether the connection goroutine and the main goroutine can interleave between the term read and the term store on the same node in a legal history\",\n        \"whether a regressed term can be observed by requestVote soon enough to yield a second vote in an already-used term\"\n      ],\n      \"assessment\": \"unassessed\",\n      \"candidate\": true,\n      \"grounding\": {\n        \"source_ids\": [\n          \"s-raft-append-term\",\n          \"s-raft-set-current-term\",\n          \"s-state-term-atomic\",\n          \"s-raft-vote-record\"\n        ],\n        \"expectation_ids\": [\n          \"s-api-fastpath-contract\",\n          \"s-integ-fastpath\"\n        ],\n        \"binding_ids\": [\n          \"bind-raft-process-heartbeat\"\n        ],\n        \"derivation\": \"appendEntries ignores an older term but adopts a greater one, and it writes the term with setCurrentTerm, which is a plain atomic Store rather than a compare-and-swap (s-raft-append-term, s-raft-set-current-term, s-state-term-atomic); api.go requires the heartbeat callback to be safe to call concurrently with a blocking RPC (s-api-fastpath-contract); NetworkTransport.handleCommand calls that callback directly from the per-connection goroutine instead of offering the RPC to the single consumer channel, and processHeartbeat forwards it to appendEntries (s-net-fastpath, s-net-handle-conn, s-raft-process-heartbeat); the heartbeat classification is decided inside the transport from the request shape, so the callback receives a request that nevertheless performs the term and leader writes. Since the adopted term is the value that requestVote evaluates against and duplicates are only recognised for the same (term, candidate) (s-raft-vote-record), a lower stored value would permit a second vote in a used term.\",\n        \"applicability\": \"Applies when a transport runs the registered heartbeat callback on a goroutine other than the raft main goroutine, which is what NetworkTransport does for heartbeat-shaped AppendEntries; it does not apply to InmemTransport, which ignores SetHeartbeatHandler.\",\n        \"unresolved\": [\n          \"whether the two goroutines can interleave between the read of currentTerm and the store inside one appendEntries call\",\n          \"whether a concurrent equal-term or greater-term main-loop RPC is required for the hazard, or a single heartbeat suffices\"\n        ],\n        \"conflicts\": [\n          \"raft.go states that processHeartbeat must only be called from the main thread while api.go states the callback MUST be safe to call concurrently with a blocking RPC\"\n        ],\n        \"alternatives\": [\n          \"the requirement may be read as 'the callback must not be blocked by the main goroutine's disk IO' rather than 'the callback may run concurrently'; under that reading the implementation is consistent and only the comment is stale\",\n          \"the atomic store may be intended to be last-writer-wins and protected in practice by the transport offering non-heartbeat RPCs to the main loop\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"version\": 1,\n      \"record\": {\n        \"path\": \"state.json\",\n        \"collection\": \"claims\",\n        \"match\": {\n          \"id\": \"c-adopted-term-never-regresses\",\n          \"version\": 1\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"artifacts\": [],\n  \"assessments\": [],\n  \"frontier\": {\n    \"relationships\": [\n      {\n        \"fact_id\": \"f-term-adopted\",\n        \"source_ids\": [\n          \"s-raft-append-term\",\n          \"s-raft-set-current-term\",\n          \"s-state-term-atomic\",\n          \"s-api-newraft-config\",\n          \"s-raft-vote-record\",\n          \"s-raft-request-vote-filter\"\n        ],\n        \"unknowns\": [\n          \"whether an out-of-band heartbeat AppendEntries can store a value lower than a term the main goroutine has already stored on the same node\"\n        ],\n        \"producers\": [\n          \"b-elect-self\",\n          \"b-term-observation\",\n          \"b-heartbeat-fastpath\",\n          \"b-newraft-recovery\"\n        ],\n        \"consumers\": [\n          \"b-follower-append-entries\",\n          \"b-follower-commit-advance\",\n          \"b-vote-grant\",\n          \"b-pre-vote-grant\",\n          \"b-term-observation\",\n          \"b-heartbeat-fastpath\",\n          \"b-leader-lease-stepdown\",\n          \"b-timeout-now-transfer\",\n          \"b-install-snapshot\"\n    